                <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
                  <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
                  <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
                    Sealing a driveway costs most homeowners <strong class="text-white">$100 to $250 in materials</strong> for a DIY weekend, or roughly $0.15 to $0.30 per square foot professionally, with the spread driven almost entirely by the number of coats and whether cracks are filled first.
                  </p>
                  <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
                    Control the number by sealing on condition rather than on a yearly schedule, filling cracks yourself before a crew arrives, and insisting that any quote you compare states coats and prep. Those three choices matter far more to the ten-year total than which brand of sealer goes down.
